#!/usr/bin/env python
"""
yt-dlp-httpd: A zero-file reverse proxy for yt-dlp streams.

SYNOPSIS
    Default Mode (Read from JSON/JSONL file or stdin):
        python yt_dlp_httpd.py <metadata.json|jsonl|- >

    Wrapper Mode (Invoke yt-dlp directly):
        yt-dlp-httpd [yt-dlp options] <URL>

DESCRIPTION
    A memory-only reverse proxy that serves streams extracted by yt-dlp.
    Uses Starlette (no Pydantic) and a shared, long-lived aiohttp session for
    maximum compatibility on ARM. Supports HTTP Range requests, automatic MIME
    mapping, upstream header forwarding, precise Content-Length / Content-Range
    synchronization from the real upstream response, HTML directory listing,
    and asyncio.Lock-protected URL refresh to prevent redundant yt-dlp calls.

DASH / requested_formats SPLIT (this revision)
    Adaptive sources (bilibili DASH, YouTube, etc.) expose a "merge placeholder"
    that has a filename and an ext but NO top-level url -- the real signed URLs
    live in `requested_formats[]` (a video-only stream plus an audio-only
    stream, each with its own headers). We now parse and split that:
      * a download with a direct `url` is served as-is (kind = "direct");
      * a placeholder with `requested_formats` is decomposed into separate
        routable streams named `<base>[<format_id>].video.<ext>` and
        `<base>[<format_id>].audio.<ext>`, each reverse-proxying its own signed
        URL and carrying the full per-stream headers (Referer is mandatory for
        bilibili or the upstream 403s). The directory listing labels them
        `DASH - video` / `DASH - audio`; a single playable file must be merged
        client-side (the proxy never muxes or touches the disk).
    Both dump shapes are handled: -J/--dump-single-json (placeholder under
    `requested_downloads[0]`) and -j/--dump-json (the top-level entry IS the
    placeholder). Refresh is idempotent per part+format_id.

ROBUST STREAM HANDLING (this revision)
    Two failure modes that a naive proxy silently mis-serves are now handled:

    1. Empty / early-closed reply. The upstream accepts the request (200/206)
       but closes the connection before delivering the byte count it declared
       (Content-Length / Content-Range). Because Starlette emits the response
       headers the moment the handler returns, a mid-stream break cannot change
       the status any more -- so the break is repaired, not reported:
         * Before any header is sent, _acquire() primes the connection by
           reading the first data chunk. If that first chunk never arrives
           (immediate EOF while bytes are expected, or a stall), the client
           has not been answered yet, so we simply reconnect / refresh here.
         * After headers are sent, body_iterator() watches the byte count. On
           truncation, a read error, or a stall it closes the connection and
           re-opens it with a Range resuming at the byte already delivered,
           stitching the remaining bytes back into the SAME stream. The client
           sees one continuous, correctly-sized response and notices nothing.

    2. Live-but-stalled connection. The socket is open yet transfers no data
       (or only absurdly little) within a given window -- the curl -y/-Y case.
       Per-read asyncio timeouts catch pure silence (STALL_TIMEOUT), and a
       sliding-window rate check catches the "few bytes trickling" case
       (SPEED_LIMIT over SPEED_TIME; SPEED_LIMIT=0 disables rate checking).

    In BOTH cases we first retry the SAME upstream URL, because a stall or an
    early close is usually a transient CDN/network hiccup that a fresh
       connection to the same URL clears. Re-invoking yt-dlp for a new URL is
    only an escalation, used after the same-URL reconnect budget is spent, and
    is further capped by MAX_URL_REFRESHES to avoid pathological loops.

ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_HOST           Bind address (default: 127.0.0.1)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_PORT           Bind port (default: 8000)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_RETRIES        Max same-URL reconnects for stream errors (default: 9)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_RETRY_DELAY    Delay in seconds between reconnects (default: 10)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_STALL_TIMEOUT  Max silence for one read / header fetch, in
                                seconds; 0 disables the silence timeout (default: 30)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_SPEED_LIMIT    Min throughput in bytes/s before a stream is
                                considered stalled (curl -Y); 0 disables rate
                                checking (default: 0)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_SPEED_TIME     Sliding window in seconds for the speed check
                                (curl -y) (default: 10)
    YT_DLP_HTTPD_MAX_REFRESH    Cap on yt-dlp URL refreshes per proxied request
                                in wrapper mode (default: 3)

REQUIREMENTS
    pip install starlette aiohttp uvicorn
"""

